{
  "mappings": [
    {
      "name": "process accepted (202, processing) -- cm.mobile and a +-prefixed number under data.phone",
      "priority": 10,
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "urlPathPattern": "/payments/[0-9a-f-]{36}",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        },
        "bodyPatterns": [
          {
            "matchesJsonPath": {
              "expression": "$.channel",
              "equalTo": "cm.mobile"
            }
          },
          {
            "matchesJsonPath": {
              "expression": "$.data.phone",
              "matches": "^\\+237[0-9]{9}$"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 202,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "body": "{\"code\":202,\"status\":\"Accepted\",\"message\":\"Payment is being processed\",\"transaction\":{\"id\":\"pay.test_{{randomValue length=12 type='ALPHANUMERIC'}}\",\"reference\":\"{{request.pathSegments.[1]}}\",\"amount\":5000,\"currency\":\"XAF\",\"status\":\"processing\"}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": [
          "openapi.yaml 2.1.0's processPayment (202). The path carries OUR reference, as the",
          "specification's example does; Notch Pay's direct-charge guide passes its own trx. reference",
          "instead, and which one the live API takes is RFC-0012 section 10 item 2, unanswered.",
          "The number goes under data.phone, the specification's first form (one guide uses",
          "data.account_number). Never confirmed against Notch Pay."
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
